Review follow-up

Decision

- GpuMemorySnapshot.kind is the sole authority for forecast memory semantics. Forecast consumes one complete snapshot instead of recomputing the kind from the host platform and reading total and usage separately.

- Windows accepts total and usage as a pair only when both describe the same source. Zero usage is valid and no longer triggers a second counter source. This prevents fabricated percentages on hybrid-GPU systems.

- Missing system measurement plus Ollama GPU allocation intentionally emits VRAM with unknown numeric values (0/0); the UI shows the accelerator without claiming a measurement.

- The Windows cfg spelling now consistently uses target_os = "windows".

